  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `reckon/run_store.py`, `reckon/file_memo.py`, `reckon/budget.py` (`_ledger_readings`, line 698), `reckon/ledger.py` (`load`, line 2758), `reckon/crew/dispatching/preparation.py` (`dispatch`, line 385) and commit `0958895bcc` (an ancestor of HEAD, and carrying `stored_run_rows`) all resolve, as does the cited profile `~/.cache/reckon-landing/station-prof-post-s107.raw`.",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 the s108 done-when (line 916) asks one project-scoped query to decode 2,000 rows that the fixture spreads across 3 projects, and gives the cache no case with two distinct argument sets.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 both arm logs sit under the run directory with a revision-and-command header and a bare `EXIT=` line; no session scratchpad or node-local path is named.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 no plan label, stage name, ticket number or version tag enters a symbol, file or comment; the section references its siblings by section id, which is the plan's own vocabulary.",
    "reasoning": "pass \u2014 the stated root cause matches the cited evidence: in `station-prof-post-s107.raw` (2,307 samples counted) `stored_run_rows` appears in 826 samples (35.8%), `_ledger_readings` 327 (14.2%), `ledger.load` 376 (16.3%) and `preparation.dispatch` 902 (39.1%), against the 35.8/14.3/16.3/39 the Why states, and the 8.9% matches the 206 plan-owned-identity samples. The endpoint is reachable and checkable: `change_token` and `store_stamp` already exist in `reckon/run_store.py` (lines 407 and 366), `stored_run_payloads` already returns a token beside lazy rows, and `stored_run_rows` decodes inline with `json.loads` on every call, so a cache and its invalidation are both measurable. The section states no implementation: it names the public query surface it measures, not a seam to extend.",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 s108 carries one deliverable, a repeated run-store query that decodes nothing while the store is unchanged.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 `s108` declares `depends-on` the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once#s107 (line 23), which is the section whose reading exposed the run-store cost and which is now `done`; `s12`, the cutover measure, now lists `s108` among its waits, so no consumer is left unheld."
  },
